/aop-runtime/aop-sealed-1000/92ef94873cd3b539011af3f1/provider-state/8c5ec6d1-e50c-4703-8e35-bc5356dee208", "/state", "--dir", "/runtime", "--dir", "/runtime/provider", "--ro-bind", "/home/mihai/.local/share/claude/versions/2.1.293", "/runtime/provider/2.1.293", "--setenv", "LANG", "en_CA.UTF-8", "--setenv", "PATH", "/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin", "--setenv", "AOP_CACHE_DIR", "/cache", "--setenv", "AOP_PROVIDER_STATE_DIR", "/state", "--setenv", "AOP_SCRATCH_DIR", "/scratch", "--setenv", "AOP_INPUT_DIR", "/inputs", "--setenv", "AOP_OUTPUT_DIR", "/output", "--setenv", "HOME", "/state/claude/home", "--setenv", "PWD", "/workspace", "--chdir", "/workspace", "--", "/runtime/provider/2.1.293", "-p", "--output-format", "stream-json", "--verbose", "--permission-mode", "bypassPermissions", "--dangerously-skip-permissions", "--add-dir", "/workspace", "--safe-mode", "--strict-mcp-config", "--mcp-config", "{\"mcpServers\":{}}", "--system-prompt", "", "--thinking-display", "summarized", "--resume", "d7c239f9-8576-4abf-b831-f490616e0298"], "duration_seconds": 39.375776, "effort": null, "error": null, "execution_completed": true, "exit_code": 0, "final_message": "I kept going and wrote `soup.py`. It runs 200 random starting grids (\"soups\") on the same 40\u00d716 wrapping board until each one starts repeating, then records when it settled and how long the repeat cycle is (its period).\n\n| Period | Soups | What's left on the board |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 57 | Only still shapes (blocks, beehives and so on) |\n| 2 | 141 | At least one blinker or other two-step oscillator |\n| 3 | 1 | A pulsar (seed 173) |\n| 32 | 1 | A single lightweight spaceship (seed 100) |\n\n- **Longest-lived soup:** seed 168 kept changing for 1,275 generations before ending as 17 still cells.\n- **Died out:** only 2 of the 200 soups ended empty.\n- **Seed 173:** produced a pulsar, a well-known 48-cell oscillator that repeats every 3 generations. The board also had a few still shapes (two blocks and a boat).\n- **Seed 100:** the 9 surviving cells are a lightweight spaceship flying vertically. It moves 2 rows every 4 generations, so it crosses the 16-row board and returns to the same position after 32 generations. That's why the period is 32: the wrapping board makes a moving object look like an oscillator.\n\nA glider couldn't do this on this board. It moves diagonally, so getting back to the same position would take 320 generations. None of the 200 soups ended with one.\n\nNext I could build a pattern classifier that names every still shape and oscillator in each final board. Or I could run thousands of soups to find rarer objects. Or I can drop this if you have something real to work on.", "finished_at": "2026-10-08T02:59:23.096114+00:00", "inference_provider": null, "inference_route": null, "inputs": [], "migration": null, "mode": "agent", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "provider": "claude", "provider_duration_seconds": null, "provider_error": null, "provider_reported_cost": null, "provider_status": null, "response_available": true, "run_id": "0bd1e381-06fd-4359-9000-d301c77525c5", "session_id": "d7c239f9-8576-4abf-b831-f490616e0298", "started_at": "2026-10-08T02:58:43.585232+00:00", "status": "succeeded", "succeeded": true, "task": "008d8b3c-7ba2-41dc-9932-a8e59ff70d26", "time_to_first_event_seconds": 0.295416, "time_to_first_response_seconds": 39.105331, "timed_out": false, "usage": {"cached_input_tokens": 46785, "input_tokens": 48751, "output_tokens": 1789, "reasoning_output_tokens": 0}, "usage_schema": "aop-token-usage-v3"}
